&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mission Brief&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As QC Inspector, you are responsible for verifying that incoming materials, manufactured parts, assemblies, and released products conform to drawings, specifications, workmanship standards, and quality requirements. You will perform dimensional and visual inspections, review supplier documentation, record objective evidence, and support reliable conformity decisions throughout incoming and final inspection.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This role is critical to protecting product quality and production continuity. You will work closely with Incoming Inspection, Production, Metrology, Supplier Quality, Manufacturing Engineering, and Product Assurance to identify non-conformances, improve inspection methods, and ensure only compliant hardware progresses through the manufacturing flow.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your Role in Our Space Mission:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform incoming and final inspections of parts, materials, assemblies, and associated documentation against approved drawings, specifications, and inspection plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct dimensional inspections using hand gauges, measurement equipment, microscopes, and coordinate measurement systems as applicable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform visual and workmanship inspections, including verification of surface condition, coating, cleaning, marking, damage, and assembly quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review certificates of conformity, inspection reports, material certificates, and other supplier quality documentation for completeness and compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Record inspection results and maintain accurate, traceable quality and product acceptance documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
